WEBVTT

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:59.090
They've created another deutera zone.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:02.010
We can stop their growth,

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:05.070
but we still can't prevent their formation.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.310
So long as the destruction
of the Gards-orm orbital base...

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.300
remains out of our reach,
we're helpless.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.810
Leave me the hell alone!

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.260
Altair's mission, complete.
Activating recovery sequence.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.260
From this point.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.200
The light armor canceler
is about to be activated.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.340
Right here!

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.070
Reconstruct the video data.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.880
What the hell is that?!
It looks just like a Zega!

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.960
A black Zega...

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.480
A new anti-Zegapain weapon
developed by the Gards-orm.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.830
They were after <i>me.</i>

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.730
Why are you so certain of that?

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.610
Transmission failure.
Her meta-body data has been lost.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.980
Ryoko Kaminagi...
has been destroyed.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:18.650
Are we going to watch it again?

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:19.840
Enough.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.920
Set air defense warning
systems to maximum level!

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.750
Repair of the Altair has top priority!

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.820
I also want all hands to thoroughly analyze
the data we have on the enemy's weapon!

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.030
<i>Any</i> clue will be helpful!

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.590
Recheck even the most trivial things!

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.670
<i>At that moment...</i>

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:43.440
<i>a bunch of words</i>
<i>were flying over my head.</i>

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.350
<i>Not just words.</i>

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.780
<i>The scenery,</i>
<i>even the passage of time...</i>

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.650
<i>Everything around me</i>
<i>just seemed to pass by.</i>

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.020
Kyo?

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.290
<i>Kaminagi had vanished.</i>

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.570
<i>There was no question</i>
<i>that she'd disappeared.</i>

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.270
<i>And yet...</i>

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.500
<i>I just couldn't understand it.</i>

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.170
Kaminagi?

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.940
I haven't seen her lately.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.780
Besides, if <i>you</i>
don't know where she is,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.980
how should I know?

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.040
Hey! Sogoru!

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.950
You need an umbrella!
You're gonna get soaked!

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.100
Ryoko?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.460
No, I haven't hung out with her lately.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:46.340
Look, now that summer break's ending,
we've got the play coming up soon.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.960
I'm kinda busy on my end, too.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:57.140
<i>It's kinda like a movie, isn't it?</i>

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:04.550
<i>The hero, having lost his lover,</i>
<i>wanders aimlessly, consumed with grief.</i>

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.020
<i>The thing is, I don't feel grief.</i>

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.200
Whatcha doing?

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.210
<i>Even now, I feel like Kaminagi...</i>

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:27.940
<i>is going to jump on</i>
<i>my back at any moment.</i>

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.660
You okay, Koji?

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:49.160
Nobody uses that room.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.090
It's your sister's room.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.170
I'm not supposed to go in there.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.370
Koji, did they?!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.480
You've erased them.
His memories.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.040
<i>I know you're watching me,</i>
<i>Mr. President!</i>

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.320
What should we do?
Should I erase the room, too?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.320
Commander, I've opened lines
to all the carrier commanders.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.100
I'll be right there.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.270
We'll have Kyo get through this.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.570
Or rather,
we'll make him get through it.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:30.600
And towards that objective...
We'll use whatever we need to.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.540
I'm coming in.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:04.700
That girl...

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.250
"The Day the World Ended."

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:26.560
A movie to remember things.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:29.890
Isn't that Maihama?

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:32.300
<i>Let's see...</i>

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.110
<i>This footage is of a summer day...</i>

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:40.470
<i>at the end of the world,</i>
<i>shot by an older student.</i>

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:45.070
<i>It's similar to the current city,</i>
<i>which exists preserved as data.</i>

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.810
<i>But it's different in some ways.</i>

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:50.280
<i>It's vanished.</i>

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:54.850
<i>And now I understand how precious</i>
<i>the world was now that it's been lost.</i>

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.760
<i>Living things seem to shine.</i>

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.260
Kaminagi...

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:03.360
<i>We take life for granted</i>
<i>while we're living it.</i>

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:08.630
<i>We aren't thankful for it.</i>
<i>We aren't glad for it, are we?</i>

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:09.910
Kaminagi!

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:12.140
<i>I guess that's just how things are.</i>

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.340
KAMINAGI!

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.410
What are you crying about?

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.290
Why?

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.350
Because the world was destroyed?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.190
Why was humanity destroyed?

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:37.500
Why do we have to fight in the Zegas?

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.300
Please, tell me why.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:42.230
What are the Gards-orm?

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.870
Why do the Gards-orm attack us?

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:49.380
Don't you think she's
pushing things a little too far?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.310
I know it's to make him work
through his grief, but still...

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:53.980
No.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:57.720
He wants a reason for
why Ryoko Kaminagi died.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:01.420
Telling him will change
his grief to anger and hatred.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.700
He'll have a target to
focus his resentment on.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:09.330
It's a psychological process
which all humans go through.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:15.310
Did I imagine it?

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.040
You shouldn't push
yourself too hard.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.870
I can't confirm a quantum
weapon reaction anywhere.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.740
Sorry to drag you out here.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.180
Oh, that's okay.
It's our duty, right?

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.610
<i>Hraesvelg, I'm here to relieve you.</i>

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:32.020
You're here early.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.420
<i>The truth is...</i>
<i>I have a favor to ask.</i>

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.350
What?

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.060
Kyo Sogoru...

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.300
Help him through this.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.130
<i>Sorry, but I won't.</i>

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.610
Like me, he's lost
the one he loves.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.100
You want me to
lick his wounds for him?

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.540
<i>No.</i>

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:56.640
You can't just lick
those wounds closed.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.490
The more they bleed, the more you
clench your teeth and bear the pain.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:02.750
You just have to conquer them!

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:08.260
You should try clenching
your teeth sometime!

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.360
I'll go talk to him.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:12.690
Lu-shen!

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.500
Bear the pain and
work through it, huh?

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.460
I don't agree.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:24.670
The death of one person can
cast a large shadow, can't it?

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:27.230
Even she's desperate now...

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.790
There are some traces which explain
the destruction of the light armor.

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.320
Tell me something
I <i>don't</i> know!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.890
I... I'm sorry.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:39.410
Look harder!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.590
Go back over all the combat data!

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:43.320
Right!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:50.490
"Toward Infinite Evolution."
"The Seven Days Program."

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.630
What the hell is this?

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:57.840
There it is!
The reason humanity was destroyed.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:02.010
Orm virus?

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.720
The Anti-Zega.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.850
As its name suggests, it renders
the Zegapain's defenses useless.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:14.790
<i>The greatest weapon</i>
<i>our holonic loaders have...</i>

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:18.020
<i>is their photonic</i>
<i>transmission technology.</i>

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:23.270
<i>It lets us form high-density photonic</i>
<i>streams into indestructible light armor,</i>

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:25.830
<i>producing a lance of light</i>
<i>which can penetrate anything.</i>

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:30.300
<i>The Zegapain was a warrior of light</i>
<i>which couldn't be wounded.</i>

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.640
However...

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.310
This thing has turned all that around.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:38.150
A warrior of darkness which
cracks light apart and rots it away!

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:42.750
<i>I propose that, from here on,</i>
<i>it be code named Anti-Zega Coatlicue.</i>

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:44.250
<i>Commander Shima!</i>

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:45.390
What?

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:46.980
<i>Look.</i>

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.090
Very well.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:05.100
Humanity was destroyed by
a virus that spread all over the world?

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.070
Impossible...

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:10.580
"The Threat of the Orm Virus."

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.140
"Data Preservation Recommendation."
Naga...

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.640
This was also written by that Naga guy?

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.320
So who the hell is Naga?!

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:18.950
Kyo.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.020
I've been trying to call you.

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:26.430
I'm not in the mood
to take any calls.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.690
When we awaken,
we always ask why we fight.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:35.330
We wonder who are these
Gards-orm that we fight against.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.700
That's the question
you've come to, isn't it?

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.110
Did Shima send you?

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:45.650
His existence is also a puzzle.

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:47.740
Forget it.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:51.240
I'll tell you as much as I know.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:53.690
It'll be faster than
your reading all that stuff.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.120
Why tell me now?

00:12:56.460 --> 00:13:00.430
Because until you decided
that you wanted to know,

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.060
the information would
have been meaningless.

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:05.920
Besides, I also want to
sort it out in my own head.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:10.500
Hey.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.410
Advance payment on my tuition.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.550
It all started with a lone
researcher named Naga.

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:27.320
The man who made the
quantum computer a reality.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.190
The I.A.L. corporation...

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:32.500
Originally established as an
information technology company,

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:34.430
they ended up branching out
into many other industries.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:38.840
They especially moved into
the bio-tech and military sectors,

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:42.430
eventually becoming a gigantic
worldwide super-conglomerate.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.130
And their CEO... was Naga.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.680
The specs of the quantum
computer he created...

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.450
made it equal by itself to the
combined processing power...

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:54.380
of all the other computers in the world.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:59.290
It was capable of housing cities,
peoples' memories,

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:02.490
even human consciousness,
within virtual space.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:05.600
Naga proposed that
humans could achieve...

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:08.730
infinite evolution within
these quantum servers.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:11.170
"Infinite evolution?"
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:15.110
To become nearly
immortal meta-bodies...

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:16.840
and in a sped up time-frame...

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:19.140
quest for endless
evolutionary development.

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:24.910
In short, to create
a Utopia for humanity.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.480
<i>Are you serious?!</i>

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:30.980
<i>It's possible,</i>
<i>thanks to the quantum computer.</i>

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:33.190
Will you excuse me?

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:34.380
I understand.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:40.090
Naga's ideals spread as the world
was electrified by his invention.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:44.360
It became a part of running the world
of finance and nations themselves.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:48.340
And then disaster struck.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:50.030
The Orm virus.

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:52.040
Exactly.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:57.050
The Orm virus raced around
the world with a 98% fatality rate.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:59.720
It was a monstrous virus,
completely destroying...

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:03.280
the genetic information of
the few infected people it left alive.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.350
It couldn't be stopped?

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.260
It was concluded
that the virus...

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.530
would completely exterminate
the human race in three years.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:17.700
Because of this, humanity was left
with no other option to survive...

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.970
than as meta-bodies
within quantum computers.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:25.730
In other words, becoming meta-bodies
was the only way to save ourselves.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.580
But, for ideological
or religious reasons,

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:32.610
many people objected
to meta-body transfer.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:34.810
The world fell into chaos.

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:38.960
Furthermore, as suspicions mounted
that the Orm virus was actually a bio-weapon,

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.860
the nations of the world
became paranoid...

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:43.630
and war broke out
across the globe.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.250
You gotta be kidding me!

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.100
While it didn't develop into
a full-scale nuclear war,

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:51.840
in only one year, we lost
seven and a half billion people.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.130
The human population dwindled to
what it was in the early 18th century.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:01.970
In the end, it took only two years for
mankind to vanish from the Earth's surface.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:05.820
The only ones left were the humans
who'd become meta-body data...

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.110
within the servers
established in each country.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:21.430
But it's said that Naga was the
one who created the Orm virus.

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.000
There's no proof.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.600
However, it's clearly specified
in Cerebrum's database.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.070
What do you mean?

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:31.000
If that really is the truth, then...

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.030
Then why did Naga
spread the virus?!

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.480
To create the Utopia
which he advocated.

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:40.850
To trap humanity inside
of the quantum servers...

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.820
as the subjects for his
experiments in infinite evolution.

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.660
He'd go that far?!

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:49.650
Naga...

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:52.890
So what happened
to this Naga guy?!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.660
If we knew that, we wouldn't
be having such a hard time.

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:59.470
He's probably a meta-body himself,
living in a server somewhere...

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:03.870
And the Gards-orm are the army
he now leads, is that it?!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.230
Yeah.

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:08.910
Once humanity was gone
from the Earth's surface,

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:12.510
I.A.L.'s production machines
began to activate.

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:16.910
It was to monopolize the Earth
completely as a test site.

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:21.990
Even now, they continue to wear away at it,
expanding their test zones.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:25.390
At the rate they're going,
they'll eventually swallow the entire world.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:29.330
Damn him.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:31.560
But then the battle began.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.870
The lab rats began to fight back.

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:40.680
Even data humans can think.
And we have defensive instincts.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.650
Rebellious elements who lived
as meta-bodies within the server.

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:46.780
People like us. In short...

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.750
The Cerebrants were born.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.760
Cerebrants.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.660
We live as warriors,

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:56.590
but we also live by
our own free will!

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.360
Don't you think so, Kyo?

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:12.030
But...

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:16.000
Kaminagi wasn't a warrior!

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.280
I swore...

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.440
I swore that I'd protect her!

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.880
She <i>was</i> a warrior.
At the very end...

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:29.790
Holonic field, forming!
Holonic blade, right hand!

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:40.500
You did great, Kaminagi!

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:41.440
You too, Kyo.

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:47.700
Kaminagi wasn't like Arque!

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:50.610
You wanted to be
with the one you loved.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:53.580
Didn't you get
your wish in the end?

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:56.640
What the hell do you
know about it?!

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.080
You can't gloss over
what happened out there!

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:04.130
For crying out loud.

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:07.060
I came off sounding
as conceited as he did.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:11.130
Lu-shen also has
high expectations for Kyo.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.740
About what?

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:15.170
Because there's
something he lacks inside.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:20.110
Because Kyo has something
that Lu-shen barely understands.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:23.250
He hopes that something
inside him will change.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:24.950
I get you.

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:27.140
I can see that, too.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:30.580
But the truth is,
that's not the real reason.

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:32.990
He just likes him.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.280
Maybe that's all it is.

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:39.420
But I wonder what will you do now?

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:44.360
The guys who stole your girlfriend away
aren't a mystery anymore, are they?

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:46.430
And that's what's pissing me off!

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:53.110
All the pain I'm burdened with,
my thoughts...

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:56.370
They're all just obstacles
designed to get me to fight?!

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.940
This is all some pre-established harmony?!

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.810
Even if it is...
I want to know what you'll do about it.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.620
And I'm telling you, I don't know!

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:14.590
He can't work through the pain
completely with someone else, huh?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.260
No, I just don't agree with it.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.530
<i>Kaminagi!</i>

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:23.700
<i>You weren't just some data stuck in here</i>
<i>to act as a pre-established harmony!</i>

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:26.740
<i>I'm sure of it! I know that you...</i>

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.970
<i>That you were alive in this world!</i>

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:31.750
KAMINAGI!!!

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:33.980
KYO!

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:36.920
What is this?!

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.520
The meta-body buffer.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:41.320
Is there a backup in that memory area?

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.160
No, I don't think so.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:45.820
Then what's this compressed file?

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:48.730
It's crash data.
I can't decode it, though.

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:54.830
Shizuno?

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.650
Shizuno, you're not?!

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:13.020
<i>Help me!</i>

00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:19.420
I finally found her.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:22.030
<i>It's Ryoko!</i>

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:25.800
<i>We found compressed data from</i>
<i>Ryoko in the Altair's memory area!</i>

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:28.330
<i>She's still alive!</i>

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:42.490
Kaminagi?

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:55.590
Time betrays us, and the world
which charges forward now freezes.

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:58.090
As though trampling everyone's
memories underfoot,

00:22:58.090 --> 00:23:00.650
these rich and peaceful
days now shatter.

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:02.930
As we're occupied
by Ryoko's resurrection,

00:23:02.930 --> 00:23:06.330
there are things
we must hurry to do now.

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:08.840
The Anti-Zega has come again!

00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:11.310
Fire it, Oceanus!
The G.A.S.P.R. cannon!

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:15.750
Next time, on Zegapain: "Reincarnation."

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:18.650
My pain, never to be forgotten.
